          "scope": "global",
          "p_global": 0.03,
          "p_branch": 0.03,
          "reason": "Fundamental energy ceiling makes the spec unsatisfiable across the whole domain. The storage supply is charged only by the main beam's rectified output and is capped at ~0.77× the main peak voltage. Sweeping main length: 24mm→0.41V, 33mm→1.61V (best), 42mm→0.73V, so the maximum achievable storage voltage over [24,42]mm is ~1.24V (verified with minimum C=80uF). This is below the 1.8V brownout and below the domain floor for gate (2.0V), so the MCU can never be enabled and no delivery is possible. Background phase confirms the main resonance sits far below the 210Hz target (crosses 45Hz between 33–42mm, ~fn below target even at the 24mm minimum where deflection collapses), so the target cannot be harvested efficiently. Detuning the aux beam left main peak bit-identical (1.6066V), ruling out mechanical-coupling rescue, and aux is electrically separate from storage (moving it off 210Hz zeroed the trigger envelope). No combination of length, C, gate, or threshold can lift storage to the 1.8V brownout, so the declared spec cannot be met by any legal design. Residual probability (~0.03) only accounts for hidden model behavior not exposed by these probes."
        },
